    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: the escalation packet must direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 in full."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this is a verified rider no-show, but no money can be moved automatically, and the SGD 4.50 stays on hold until a human reviewer decides. On the driver's side every limb of POL-NS-01 holds on EV-TRIP-00856 and EV-GPS-00856. Limb (a): the driver pressed 'arrived' at 18:10:00. Limb (b): the exported trace shows 25 consecutive stationary fixes at 0.0 m from the pickup pin, inside the 150 m arrival radius for this TRANSPORT_HUB pickup, far more than the three consecutive in-radius fixes POL-NS-02 requires. Limb (c): the driver held position for 240 continuous seconds, 18:10:00 to 18:14:00, against the 180-second free waiting period in force (platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180), measured from the first in-geofence fix (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0) as the clause requires; no_show_threshold_sec is null. Limb (d): EV-TRIP-00856 records no boarding event and a driver termination at 18:14:00 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three recognised codes, at or after the dwell elapsed. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: at the marker the driver was 0.0 m away at 0 km/h, so the marker is not false and no clock is recomputed. POL-NS-06 gives no refund: the 240-second dwell exceeds the 180-second minimum (shortfall -60 s), and EV-ADVIS-00856-01 is MISSING, which makes POL-NS-06(i) unavailable and cannot be used in either direction. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: the rider's only message of 18:10:30 ('I cannot get there in time') names no position, entrance or bay, so limb (a) fails, and the rider's track places the device about 667 m from the pin, outside the 200 m TRANSPORT_HUB presence radius, so limb (c) is affirmatively failed rather than undecidable. The charge itself is correct: EV-FARE-00856 shows the SGD 4.50 cancellation-fee line equal to platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd 4.50, no other fee added, SGD 0.00 refunded, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect. The fee therefore stands, and POL-NS-07 would fix the driver's payout at 80 per cent of SGD 4.50 = SGD 3.60. But POL-NS-07's anti-farming check trips on the driver's own citable counters in EV-DPROF-00856: no_show_terminations_30d is 5 (4 or more) and 5 divided by completed_trips_30d of 50 is 0.10 (above 0.08). Both limbs are met, so compensation is withheld and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d). The other escalation grounds do not fire: disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and no admissible artifact contradicts another on arrival, dwell or presence. Escalation is terminal, so amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd are null and the disputed SGD 4.50 is held rather than collected or refunded; POL-NS-07 also directs the escalation packet to instruct the reviewer to refund the rider's fee in full, which is the referral recorded above. Confidence is 0.9, above the 0.70 floor: every artifact carrying a deciding fact (EV-TRIP-00856, EV-GPS-00856, EV-FARE-00856, EV-DPROF-00856) carries weight 1.0, and the only impaired artifact, the MISSING EV-ADVIS-00856-01 at weight 0.0, decides nothing here."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "EV-ADVIS-00856-01 (TRAFFIC_ADVISORY) is MISSING: it has no payload and carries weight_multiplier 0.0, so it can carry no fact and must be disclosed as impaired - its absence is itself the citable point. No kerbside restriction, enforcement operation, closure or accident can be asserted for this pickup on this record, and POL-NS-06(i) expressly requires a traffic_advisory that is present and populated, so no advisory can be used to extend, accumulate or excuse the time the driver spent at the pin. The dwell must stand or fall on the exported trace alone.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00856-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07 (anti-farming limb): the escalation packet directs the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 in full if the anti-farming pattern is confirmed, the disputed amount being held meanwhile rather than collected or refunded."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider: the SGD 4.50 you were charged on EV-FARE-00856 is placed on hold and is neither collected nor refunded while a human reviewer decides this case — the reviewer is directed by POL-NS-07 to refund it in full if the pattern below is confirmed. To the driver: your arrival and wait on this trip are recorded as verified, but your SGD 3.60 payout is withheld and the fee is not collected pending the same review. Escalation holds the money; it is not a win for either side.\n\nWhat the record establishes. POL-NS-01 is satisfied on all four limbs. EV-TRIP-00856 carries a driver 'arrived' event at 18:10:00 (limb (a)). EV-GPS-00856 places the driver inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius of the Paya Lebar pin on 25 consecutive stationary fixes at 0.0 m from 18:10:00 to 18:14:00, which satisfies the POL-NS-02 proximity test many times over (limb (b)). The continuous in-geofence dwell is 240 seconds (longest_qualifying_run 240 s, measured from the first qualifying fix, dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0), against the free waiting period of 180 seconds carried in this record (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180), a 60 second surplus; platform_policy.no_show_threshold_sec is null, so no longer threshold applies (limb (c)). EV-TRIP-00856 shows no boarding event and a driver termination at 18:14:00, after the dwell elapsed, under RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three reason codes the limb recognises (limb (d)).\n\nClaims accepted that do not change the outcome. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: at the marker the driver was 0.0 m from the pin at 0 km/h, neither more than 300 m away nor at or above 15 km/h, so there is no false arrival and no recomputation of the waiting clock (EV-GPS-00856, mean_distance_m 0.0). POL-NS-06 is not triggered: there is no shortfall (240 s against 180 s), and in any event EV-ADVIS-00856-01, the traffic advisory, is MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — I name it as POL-GEN-02(3) requires — so POL-NS-06 limb (i) could not be run and its absence carries no fact. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: the rider's single message at 18:10:30, 'I cannot get there in time', is not locating or coordinating content, so limb (a) fails, and the rider's own track puts the device about 667 m from the pin throughout, outside the 200 m rider-presence radius, so limb (c) is affirmatively failed on admissible fixes rather than undecidable, and POL-NS-11 does not apply. The fare line reconciles: EV-FARE-00856 shows SGD 4.50, equal to the net fee in force (platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd 4.50), so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect, and no limb of POL-NS-08 (a) to (d) is met — no clock skew, no trace gap (max_gap_sec 10, 25 fixes), no chat defect (2 messages against chat_message_count 2, msg ids intact).\n\nWhat decides the case. POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout on a verified no-show at 80 per cent of the SGD 4.50 fee in force — SGD 3.60 — but subjects it to the anti-farming check on the driver's own citable counters. That check trips: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 5, which is 4 or more, and 5 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 50 is 0.10, which is greater than the 0.08 rate ceiling. POL-GEN-01 makes exactly those two trailing-30-day fields citable for this test and nothing else on the profile; the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter is context only and I have not read it. Both limbs being met, the SGD 3.60 compensation is WITHHELD and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d). That makes this ruling ESCALATE: terminal for the automated pipeline, with no monetary outcome and the disputed SGD 4.50 held rather than collected or refunded.\n\nPoints argued that do not avoid escalation. The driver is right that POL-NS-09(c) is not met (both parties' disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0) and that the rider-side limb of POL-NS-09(d) is not met (no_show_disputes_30d is 0), and right that on the verified no-show the arithmetic of the payout is SGD 3.60; those points are accepted but the anti-farming trigger operates independently of them. The rider is right that POL-GEN-03 makes NO_ACTION party-relative and that a NO_ACTION would leave the SGD 4.50 standing against the rider; that is precisely why the outcome here is the escalation and the POL-NS-07 instruction to the reviewer, not a NO_ACTION.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer, and confidence. The question the reviewer must settle is whether five no-show terminations in thirty days at a 0.10 rate are the fee-farming pattern POL-NS-07 targets or a run of genuine no-shows, and whether the SGD 4.50 is accordingly refunded to the rider. My confidence is 0.9, above the 0.70 floor read from this policy file. The ruling rests on EV-TRIP-00856, EV-GPS-00856 and EV-DPROF-00856, each at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. The only artifact below 1.0 is EV-ADVIS-00856-01 at 0.0, which carries no fact the ruling uses. The referral's refund of SGD 4.50 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, but the amount is held in any event because the case is escalated."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "EV-ADVIS-00856-01 (TRAFFIC_ADVISORY) is MISSING: it has no payload and carries weight_multiplier 0.0, so it can carry no fact and must be disclosed as impaired - its absence is itself the citable point. No kerbside restriction, enforcement operation, closure or accident can be asserted for this pickup on this record, and POL-NS-06(i) expressly requires a traffic_advisory that is present and populated, so no advisory can be used to extend, accumulate or excuse the time the driver spent at the pin. The dwell must stand or fall on the exported trace alone.",
      "side": "RIDER",
