    "explanation": "This was a genuine no-show on the driver's evidence, but the driver's own 30-day record sends the case to human review. On the merits, POL-NS-01 (a)-(d) are all satisfied at weight 1.0: EV-TRIP-00856 carries the driver 'arrived' event at 2026-09-16 18:10:00 (limb a) and a driver termination at 18:14:00 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event (limb d); EV-GPS-00856 places the driver at 0.0 m from the pickup pin for 240 continuous seconds across 25 stationary fixes from 18:10:00 to 18:14:00 (limbs b and c), well inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius and 60 seconds beyond the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180; no_show_threshold_sec is null). The arrival marker is not false: 0.0 m and 0 km/h at the marker, so POL-NS-05 is not engaged, and there is no dwell shortfall, so POL-NS-06 gives no refund route (EV-ADVIS-00856-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, but it is not needed: the 240-second dwell already exceeds the minimum and only one in-geofence interval exists). POL-NS-04 does not help the rider: the rider's 18:10:30 message 'I cannot get there in time' names no position or entrance (limb a fails) and the rider's device sat about 667 m from the pin, outside the 200 m rider-presence radius, with zero qualifying fixes (limb c affirmatively failed, so POL-NS-11 does not apply). EV-FARE-00856 correctly shows the SGD 4.50 fee and SGD 0.00 refunded, reconciling with the net fee in force, so POL-NS-08(d) is clean. The decisive point is the driver's own profile: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 5 (at or above the threshold of 4) and 5 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 50 is 0.10 (above the 0.08 rate limb). Both limbs of the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check therefore trip on the two fields POL-GEN-01 makes citable for that test, the SGD 3.60 payout (80 per cent of SGD 4.50) is WITHHELD, and POL-NS-07 and POL-NS-09(d) escalate the case. There is no repeat-pairing or rider-side abuse escalation: both disputes_with_counterparty_90d fields are 0 and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, so POL-NS-09(c) and the rider limb of (d) are not met. ESCALATE is terminal, so no money moves: the disputed SGD 4.50 is held, not collected and not refunded, and both money fields are null. The escalation packet directs the reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.50 in full so the rider does not fund an unresolved dispute. Monetary effect is moot under POL-GEN-05 because escalation issues no monetary ruling."
